    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Chanda Mama, the Moon, is sometimes round like a circle and sometimes a different shape.\nHe started counting the stars. 1, 2, 3, 10, 21, 45, 99, 100 and on to 999, and then he yawned and fell asleep.\nIn the morning the Sun peeped out, and Chanda Mama woke in the evening. He started again but forgot where he had stopped.\nNight after night he counted and often forgot the count.\nOne night he was upset and began to cry, because he could never finish. The Sun saw his tears and smiled.\nThe Sun said he could tell him how many stars there are. His answer connects the stars to lovely children, which you will read in your book.\nThe story is about counting and wondering at the sky.\nNew words: yawn, count, forgot."
    }
